{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"756","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Bacterial Melee"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Julia is conducting an experiment in her lab. She placed several luminescent bacterial colonies in a horizontal testtube. Different types of bacteria can be distinguished by the color of light they emit. Julia marks types of bacteria with small Latin letters \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", ..., \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"z"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The testtube is divided into "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" consecutive regions. Each region is occupied by a single colony of a certain bacteria type at any given moment. Hence, the population of the testtube at any moment can be described by a string of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" Latin characters."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Sometimes a colony can decide to conquer another colony in one of the adjacent regions. When that happens, the attacked colony is immediately eliminated and replaced by a colony of the same type as the attacking colony, while the attacking colony keeps its type. Note that a colony can only attack its neighbours within the boundaries of the testtube. At any moment, at most one attack can take place."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For example, consider a testtube with population \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"babb"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\". There are six options for an attack that may happen next:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the first colony attacks the second colony ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 → 2"},{"kind":"text","text":"), the resulting population is \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"bbbb"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\";"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2 → 1"},{"kind":"text","text":", the result is \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"aabb"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\";"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2 → 3"},{"kind":"text","text":", the result is \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"baab"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\";"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3 → 2"},{"kind":"text","text":", the result is \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"bbbb"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" (note that the result is the same as the first option);"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3 → 4"},{"kind":"text","text":" or "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"4 → 3"},{"kind":"text","text":", the population does not change."}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The pattern of attacks is rather unpredictable. Julia is now wondering how many different configurations of bacteria in the testtube she can obtain after a sequence of attacks takes place (it is possible that no attacks will happen at all). Since this number can be large, find it modulo "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"109 + 7"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains an integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" — the number of regions in the testtube ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ n ≤ 5 000"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" small Latin letters that describe the initial population of the testtube."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print one number — the answer to the problem modulo "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"109 + 7"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3\naaa\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2\nab\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4\nbabb\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"11\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"7\nabacaba\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"589\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first sample the population can never change since all bacteria are of the same type."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second sample three configurations are possible: \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ab"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" (no attacks), \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"aa"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" (the first colony conquers the second colony), and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"bb"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" (the second colony conquers the first colony)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"To get the answer for the third sample, note that more than one attack can happen."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"D","problemCode":"756D","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/756/problem/D"}